hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17349","Haddathana Haywah ibn Shurayh and Yazid ibn Abd Rabbih, they said haddathana Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid, haddathani Bahir ibn Sad, from Khalid ibn Madan, haddathana Jubayr ibn Nufayr, that Umar al-Jumai narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah wants good for a servant, He employs him before his death. A man from the people asked him: What is His employing him. He said: Allah, Exalted is He, guides him to righteous work before his death, then seizes him upon that."
